--- secp256k1 security note ---
  SPLIT cases: Jac≅E₁×E₂ where E₁,E₂ have CM by Q(√-D_cm)
  Family D=3 (sf=3): CM by Z[ω], j=0 — same CM field as secp256k1!
  HCDLP on these Jacobians reduces to ECDLP on j=0 curves over F_p.
  All j=0 curves have orders p+1±t where 4p=t²+3 (⇒ #E≡0 mod 3),
  so Pohlig-Hellman takes out the 3-part. For p≥7, #E≥7, safe.
  STRUCTURAL COMPLETENESS THEOREM unaffected: secp256k1 (p=2²⁵⁶-2³²-977)
  has p≡7 mod 12, and 4p=t²+3 would need t²=4p-3≈2²⁵⁸, impossible for
  integer t in a feasible computation.
